{
  "dom_id": "step-e3639",
  "name": "Example: Differentiating a Quotient Using Leibniz Notation",
  "problem": "Given that $y=\\dfrac{1}{3x+7},$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $u=1$ and $v=3x+7.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\t& = \\dfrac{ v\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}-u\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x}}{v^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t& = \\dfrac{ \\left( 3x+7 \\right ) \\cdot 0 -1\\cdot 3}{\\left( 3x+7\\right)^2}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t& = -\\dfrac{3}{\\left( 3x+7\\right)^2}.\n\t\t}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
